{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.MassVolDensity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.MassVolDensity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Mass.SaddleQShiftOffset"],"declarations":29,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.so3_adjoint_eq_one_plus_two_cosh_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.so3_adjoint_eq_one_plus_two_cosh_two","kind":"theorem","line":369,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MassVolDensity.lean#L369-L373","doc":"The SO(3)_q adjoint in the U(1) hyperbolic shadow: `[3]_q = 1 + 2 cosh(2η)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.so3_adjoint_eq_chebyshev","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.so3_adjoint_eq_chebyshev","kind":"theorem","line":360,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MassVolDensity.lean#L360-L367","doc":"**The SO(3)_q adjoint is the Chebyshev square of the SU(2)_q doublet:\n`[3]_q = [2]_q² − 1`.** This is the ℤ₂-quotient level structure —\nthe j=1 (integer-spin) character is the symmetric-square-minus-trivial\nof the j=½ doublet, the lowest irrep surviving SO(3) = SU(2)/ℤ₂. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.so3_adjoint_eq_four_cosh_sq_sub_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.so3_adjoint_eq_four_cosh_sq_sub_one","kind":"theorem","line":350,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MassVolDensity.lean#L350-L358","doc":"Closed form `[3]_q = 4 cosh²η − 1` (for `sinh η ≠ 0`), via\n`sinh(3η) = sinh η · (4 sinh²η + 3)` and `sinh²η = cosh²η − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.so3_adjoint_character","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.so3_adjoint_character","kind":"def","line":344,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MassVolDensity.lean#L344-L348","doc":"SO(3)_q adjoint (vector, j=1) Weyl character `χ_1(η) = sinh(3η)/sinh η`\n(the `[3]_q` quantum integer at `q = e^η`). The lowest integer-spin\nirrep, i.e. the lowest one descending through SO(3) = SU(2)/ℤ₂. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.su2_fundamental_eq_two_cosh","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.su2_fundamental_eq_two_cosh","kind":"theorem","line":305,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MassVolDensity.lean#L305-L313","doc":"**The fundamental SU(2)_q character is the U(1) doublet `2 cosh η`.**\nThis is the bridge: the abelian cosh is the j=½ SU(2) character, so the\nrecurring `[2]_q ≈ 2.0109` weight is simultaneously the doublet\nSU(2) character and `2 cosh(log q₀)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.su2_fundamental_character","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.su2_fundamental_character","kind":"def","line":300,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MassVolDensity.lean#L300-L303","doc":"SU(2)_q fundamental Weyl character `χ_{1/2}(η) = sinh(2η)/sinh η`\n(the j=½ doublet; `[2]_q` at `q = e^η`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.binding_difference_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.binding_difference_odd","kind":"theorem","line":272,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MassVolDensity.lean#L272-L278","doc":"**Binding parity (odd):** the mirror difference flips sign under the\nmirror flip `θ_B ↦ −θ_B`. Hence — exactly as for the p-n mass split — a\nδ² (even) correction is parity-FORBIDDEN on ΔB and allowed only on the\n(M_λ-gated) average. The quadratic-δ consistency check, for binding. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.binding_mirror_average_eq_cosh","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.binding_mirror_average_eq_cosh","kind":"theorem","line":263,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MassVolDensity.lean#L263-L270","doc":"**Mirror binding average is `B₀·cosh θ_B`** — the EVEN channel (the\nabsolute scale, which the per-block M_λ gate blocks). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.binding_mirror_difference_eq_sinh","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.binding_mirror_difference_eq_sinh","kind":"theorem","line":253,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MassVolDensity.lean#L253-L261","doc":"**Mirror binding difference is `2·B₀·sinh θ_B`** — the ODD channel: the\nM_λ-gate sidestep. The antisymmetric (difference) content is `sinh`, so\nit is computable from the difference alone, before the absolute average. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.binding_mirror_high","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.binding_mirror_high","kind":"def","line":250,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MassVolDensity.lean#L250-L251","doc":"³He-side binding as `B₀·e^{+θ_B}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.binding_mirror_low","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.binding_mirror_low","kind":"def","line":247,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MassVolDensity.lean#L247-L248","doc":"³H-side binding as `B₀·e^{−θ_B}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.pn_rapidity_leading","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.pn_rapidity_leading","kind":"def","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MassVolDensity.lean#L224-L227","doc":"The leading p-n rapidity `θ = δ/2`, so `e^{∓θ} ≈ 1 ∓ δ/2` recovers the\nproduction linear split at O(δ); the exact θ carries the higher odd-δ\ntower (sinh) with no even contamination. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.mass_split_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.mass_split_odd","kind":"theorem","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MassVolDensity.lean#L216-L222","doc":"**Parity (odd): the split flips sign under p↔n (θ ↦ −θ).** Hence a δ²\n(even) correction is parity-FORBIDDEN on Δ_pn — only odd powers of θ\n(δ¹, δ³, …) may appear. This is the formal statement of the\nquadratic-δ consistency check. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.mass_avg_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.mass_avg_even","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MassVolDensity.lean#L210-L214","doc":"**Parity (even): m_avg is invariant under p↔n (θ ↦ −θ).** Hence a δ²\ncorrection is parity-allowed on the average. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.mass_split_eq_sinh","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.mass_split_eq_sinh","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MassVolDensity.lean#L202-L208","doc":"**Half the mass split is `m₀·sinh θ`** (ODD in θ ⇒ carries every odd-δ\ncorrection; the antisymmetric Δ_pn channel). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.mass_avg_eq_cosh","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.mass_avg_eq_cosh","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MassVolDensity.lean#L194-L200","doc":"**Average mass is `m₀·cosh θ`** (EVEN in θ ⇒ carries every even-δ\ncorrection; the m_avg channel). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.mass_neutron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.mass_neutron","kind":"def","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MassVolDensity.lean#L191-L192","doc":"Neutron mass as the opposite rotation `m₀·e^{+θ}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.mass_proton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.mass_proton","kind":"def","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MassVolDensity.lean#L188-L189","doc":"Proton mass as a hyperbolic rotation `m₀·e^{−θ}` by the p-n rapidity θ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.bracket_2_q_eq_two_cosh_log","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.bracket_2_q_eq_two_cosh_log","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MassVolDensity.lean#L179-L186","doc":"**`[2]_q = 2·cosh(log q)`** — the doublet integer is the *even*\nhyperbolic function of the rapidity. At q₀ this is the recurring\n`≈ 2.0109` Hecke/HOMFLY weight. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.h_crossing_eq_two_sinh_log","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.h_crossing_eq_two_sinh_log","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MassVolDensity.lean#L171-L177","doc":"**`h = 2·sinh(log q)`** — the Hecke crossing scale is the *odd*\nhyperbolic function of the rapidity `η = log q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.bracket_2_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.bracket_2_q","kind":"def","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MassVolDensity.lean#L167-L169","doc":"The doublet quantum integer `[2]_q = q + q⁻¹` (local copy of\n`HadronicMass.bracket_2_q`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.pn_crossing_coeff_color_blind","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.pn_crossing_coeff_color_blind","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MassVolDensity.lean#L132-L141","doc":"Sanity: at the color-blind limit `δ = 0` the interface crossing\ncoefficient is the symmetric average `−h/2` (the `strict_averaged`\nconvention). Stated as the `δ ↦ 0` specialisation; the genuine\n`delta_subleading q = 0` only at `q = 1` (unknot/trivial limit), which\nis the one place the algebraic and hyperbolic pictures must agree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.pn_crossing_coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.pn_crossing_coeff","kind":"def","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MassVolDensity.lean#L124-L130","doc":"The p-n interface crossing coefficient `d(q) = −h·(½ − δ/4)` of the\ncolor-weighted averaged crossing `σ + d·𝟙` (here δ = `delta_subleading`).\nThis is the algebraic object whose holonomy P3 will identify with the\nnon-abelian-Stokes interface curvature; recording it as a `def` fixes\nthe target of that derivation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.delta_subleading","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.delta_subleading","kind":"def","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MassVolDensity.lean#L115-L122","doc":"**δ subleading** = `δ_leading · (1 + ℏ_q³)` — the full flavor split\nwith the 3-loop substrate-Planck correction (`flavor_split_subleading`\nin `_li_2_q_util.py`; matches `_avg_color_delta()` to 2.6e-19). The\nfactor `(1 + ℏ_q³)` is the algebraic image of the 3-loop term in the\nsurface-ordered (non-abelian Stokes) holonomy expansion — see the P3/P4\nfollow-up. Still purely algebraic in `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.delta_leading_eq_closed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.delta_leading_eq_closed","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MassVolDensity.lean#L104-L113","doc":"**δ leading agrees with the existing closed polynomial form.**\n\n`(q − 1)²·(1 − q⁻⁴)/3 = (q − 1)²·(q⁴ − 1)/(3 q⁴)`.\n\nPins `delta_leading` to `HadronicMass.delta_m_over_M_N_substrate`\nwithout importing it. Pure algebra (`field_simp; ring`, `q ≠ 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.delta_leading","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.delta_leading","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MassVolDensity.lean#L97-L102","doc":"**δ leading** = `(q − 1)²·(1 − q⁻⁴)/3` — the substrate flavor split\n`Δm/M_N` at leading order (`prop:flavor-split-substrate`). Equal to the\nexisting `HadronicMass.delta_m_over_M_N_substrate q = (q−1)²(q⁴−1)/(3q⁴)`\nvia `1 − q⁻⁴ = (q⁴ − 1)/q⁴`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.density_borromean_eq_linking_weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.density_borromean_eq_linking_weight","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MassVolDensity.lean#L75-L88","doc":"**P2′ — density agrees with the `5/2 + 3h²/4` linking-weight form.**\n\n`(3 q² + 4 + 3 q⁻²) / 4 = 5/2 + 3·(q − q⁻¹)² / 4`.\n\nHand-check: `(q − q⁻¹)² = q² − 2 + q⁻²`, so `3(q−q⁻¹)²/4 =\n(3q² − 6 + 3q⁻²)/4`, and `5/2 + that = (10 + 3q² − 6 + 3q⁻²)/4 =\n(3q² + 4 + 3q⁻²)/4`. Pure algebra; `field_simp; ring` after `q ≠ 0`.\nThis is the bridge between the `q`-power density and the `lwA` form\n(`QOU/BraidKnot/TwoRoutesProtonMass.lean`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.density_borromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.density_borromean","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MassVolDensity.lean#L63-L73","doc":"**Density ρ(q)** for the Borromean nucleon 𝓑₃ — the Family-A Hecke\nlinking weight, in the manifestly symmetric `q`-power form\n\n  `ρ(q) = (3 q² + 4 + 3 q⁻²) / 4`.\n\nThis is the energy density that multiplies `Vol(𝓑₃)/ℏ_q²` in the mass\nformula; it is the partition-weighted Markov trace `Σ_λ y_λ χ^λ(𝓑₃)`\n(the Wedderburn form `(1/4) Σ_{λ⊢4} dim_q V_λ` is proved in\n`QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanMarkovTrace.lean`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.h_crossing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.h_crossing","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MassVolDensity.lean#L60-L61","doc":"The Hecke crossing scale `h = q − q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}